{"code":"34576173","hash":"6abd39205dd7460b898d84d0","playerName":"hocTA73129","room":{"code":"34576173","assignments":null,"createdAt":1790785824492,"scheduledAt":null,"deleted":false,"experiment":"main_main","hash":"6abd39205dd7460b898d84d0","hostId":"690381fad70ac7916cf6a8c9","hostSessionId":"5f272590-064e-4626-ae2e-bf6c3e0a31d6","hostOccupation":"personal","canvas":{"host":false,"player":false,"annotations":false},"name":"MOUNTAIN","options":{"accommodations":"no","showAnswers_2":"always","studentQuizReview_2":"yes","redemption":"no","powerups":"no","loginRequired":false,"jumble":false,"jumbleAnswers":true,"showAnswers":true,"studentQuizReview":true,"studentLeaderboard":false,"timer":false,"timer_3":"off","memes":false,"memeset":"66ffb7ce6c18f9cf20f405f5","studentMusic":false,"limitAttempts":0,"nicknameGenerator":false,"extraLife":"","scheduleLater":false,"gameRunningDuration":-1,"reduceMotion":false,"showGameCountdown":true,"showGameSummary":true,"showPlayerAttemptDetails":true,"isIcebreakerQuiz":false,"assignOnGCAddon":false,"hasRedemptionPass":"no","allowIssues":false,"isMasteryPeakTimerEnabled":false,"adaptive":false,"mandatoryRosterName":false,"areHintsEnabled":false,"skipQuestion":false,"preventSkipping":true,"videoSpeed":false,"captionsEnabled":false,"isNoFrills":false,"antiCheating":{"enabled":true,"alertOnInfraction":false,"disableRightClick":false,"disableCopyPaste":false},"readAloud":false,"calculator":false,"fourFnCalculator":false,"graphing":false,"dontRewardMarksForUngradableQuestions":false,"showReferenceNotes":false,"stickyNotepad":false,"globalNotepad":false,"protractor":false},"questions":{"69ca8be11ec7da8253f2063e":{"structure":{"settings":{"hasCorrectAnswer":true,"fibDataType":"string","canSubmitCustomResponse":false,"doesOptionHaveMultipleTargets":false,"showAdvancedRTE":false},"hasMath":false,"query":{"type":null,"hasMath":false,"math":{"latex":[],"template":null},"answerTime":-1,"text":"<p>TOPIC: <strong>MOUNTAIN</strong></p><p><strong>For centuries, towering peaks were treated as silent opponents in a contest of strength. To plant a flag on the summit was to declare victory over nature itself. Yet this image is slowly fading. Many climbers now describe mountains less as enemies and more as companions—spaces for thought, culture, and fragile ecosystems. The vocabulary of conquest has given way to that of respect. A climb is no longer measured only by height gained, but by insight and connection found along the way.</strong></p>","media":[]},"options":[{"type":"text","hasMath":false,"math":{"latex":[],"template":null},"answerTime":0,"id":"68c84a25776684eb0cdda650","text":"<p><strong>Redefining the concept of a mountain/ People’s perspective of mountain (Thay đổi định nghĩa về núi)</strong></p>","media":[],"_id":"68c84a25776684eb0cdda650"},{"type":"text","hasMath":false,"math":{"latex":[],"template":null},"answerTime":0,"id":"68c84a25776684eb0cdda651","text":"<p><strong>The unique feeling of achievement (Cảm giác độc đáo khi đạt đc thành tựu)</strong></p>","media":[],"_id":"68c84a25776684eb0cdda651"},{"type":"text","hasMath":false,"math":{"latex":[],"template":null},"answerTime":0,"id":"68c84a25776684eb0cdda652","text":"<p><strong>Public recognition of accomplishments (Danh tiếng từ thành tựu)</strong></p>","media":[],"_id":"68c84a25776684eb0cdda652"},{"type":"text","hasMath":false,"math":{"latex":[],"template":null},"answerTime":0,"id":"68c84a25776684eb0cdda653","text":"<p><strong>The mistake of misplaced priorities (Sự ưu tiên sai lầm)</strong></p>","media":[],"_id":"68c84a25776684eb0cdda653"},{"type":"text","hasMath":false,"math":{"latex":[],"template":null},"answerTime":0,"id":"68c84b0f776684eb0cdda667","text":"<p><strong>A concerning connection/ Disturbing relevance (Mối liên quan đáng lo ngại)</strong></p>","media":[],"_id":"68c84b0f776684eb0cdda667"}],"explain":{},"hints":[],"kind":"MCQ","marks":{"correct":1,"incorrect":0}},"topics":[],"unifiedStandardIds":[],"cloned":true,"ver":2,"_id":"69ca8be11ec7da8253f2063e","time":45000,"type":"MCQ","createdAt":"2026-03-30T14:42:41.260Z","updated":"2026-03-30T14:42:41.273Z","state":"inactive","attempt":0},"69ca8bdb7482e546520c1f93":{"structure":{"settings":{"hasCorrectAnswer":true,"fibDataType":"string","canSubmitCustomResponse":false,"doesOptionHaveMultipleTargets":false,"showAdvancedRTE":false},"hasMath":false,"query":{"type":null,"hasMath":false,"math":{"latex":[],"template":null},"answerTime":-1,"text":"<p>TOPIC: <strong>MOUNTAIN</strong></p><p><strong>Those who have stood at the top often struggle to explain the moment. The thin air sharpens the senses, the vast view stretches imagination, and the relief of arrival overwhelms words. The experience feels unlike any finish line on earth. Some compare it to winning a race, yet most insist the emotions are deeper, rooted in both exhaustion and discovery. Long after they return, climbers carry the memory as a reminder that persistence can transform impossible walls into unforgettable horizons.</strong></p>","media":[]},"options":[{"type":"text","hasMath":false,"math":{"latex":[],"template":null},"answerTime":0,"id":"68c84a25776684eb0cdda650","text":"<p><strong>Redefining the concept of a mountain/ People’s perspective of mountain (Thay đổi định nghĩa về núi)</strong></p>","media":[],"_id":"68c84a25776684eb0cdda650"},{"type":"text","hasMath":false,"math":{"latex":[],"template":null},"answerTime":0,"id":"68c84a25776684eb0cdda651","text":"<p><strong>The unique feeling of achievement (Cảm giác độc đáo khi đạt đc thành tựu)</strong></p>","media":[],"_id":"68c84a25776684eb0cdda651"},{"type":"text","hasMath":false,"math":{"latex":[],"template":null},"answerTime":0,"id":"68c84a25776684eb0cdda652","text":"<p><strong>Public recognition of accomplishments (Danh tiếng từ thành tựu)</strong></p>","media":[],"_id":"68c84a25776684eb0cdda652"},{"type":"text","hasMath":false,"math":{"latex":[],"template":null},"answerTime":0,"id":"68c84a25776684eb0cdda653","text":"<p><strong>The mistake of misplaced priorities (Sự ưu tiên sai lầm)</strong></p>","media":[],"_id":"68c84a25776684eb0cdda653"},{"type":"text","hasMath":false,"math":{"latex":[],"template":null},"answerTime":0,"id":"68c84b0f776684eb0cdda667","text":"<p><strong>A concerning connection/ Disturbing relevance (Mối liên quan đáng lo ngại)</strong></p>","media":[],"_id":"68c84b0f776684eb0cdda667"}],"explain":{},"hints":[],"kind":"MCQ","marks":{"correct":1,"incorrect":0}},"topics":[],"unifiedStandardIds":[],"cloned":true,"ver":2,"_id":"69ca8bdb7482e546520c1f93","time":45000,"type":"MCQ","createdAt":"2026-03-30T14:42:35.593Z","updated":"2026-03-30T14:42:35.605Z","state":"inactive","attempt":0},"69ca8be60529b06e80c78c84":{"structure":{"settings":{"hasCorrectAnswer":true,"fibDataType":"string","canSubmitCustomResponse":false,"doesOptionHaveMultipleTargets":false,"showAdvancedRTE":false},"hasMath":false,"query":{"type":null,"hasMath":false,"math":{"latex":[],"template":null},"answerTime":-1,"text":"<p>TOPIC: <strong>MOUNTAIN</strong></p><p><strong>Fame has a way of turning private journeys into public spectacles. A solitary ascent of a distant peak may suddenly be printed in newspapers, retold in books, or adapted for film. Recognition can inspire others and bring attention to larger causes, but it also changes the climber’s relationship with the mountain. The expectation of new records or riskier attempts can weigh heavily. What began as personal exploration may, under society’s gaze, become performance—measured not by meaning, but by applause.</strong></p>","media":[]},"options":[{"type":"text","hasMath":false,"math":{"latex":[],"template":null},"answerTime":0,"id":"68c84a25776684eb0cdda650","text":"<p><strong>Redefining the concept of a mountain/ People’s perspective of mountain (Thay đổi định nghĩa về núi)</strong></p>","media":[],"_id":"68c84a25776684eb0cdda650"},{"type":"text","hasMath":false,"math":{"latex":[],"template":null},"answerTime":0,"id":"68c84a25776684eb0cdda651","text":"<p><strong>The unique feeling of achievement (Cảm giác độc đáo khi đạt đc thành tựu)</strong></p>","media":[],"_id":"68c84a25776684eb0cdda651"},{"type":"text","hasMath":false,"math":{"latex":[],"template":null},"answerTime":0,"id":"68c84a25776684eb0cdda652","text":"<p><strong>Public recognition of accomplishments (Danh tiếng từ thành tựu)</strong></p>","media":[],"_id":"68c84a25776684eb0cdda652"},{"type":"text","hasMath":false,"math":{"latex":[],"template":null},"answerTime":0,"id":"68c84a25776684eb0cdda653","text":"<p><strong>The mistake of misplaced priorities (Sự ưu tiên sai lầm)</strong></p>","media":[],"_id":"68c84a25776684eb0cdda653"},{"type":"text","hasMath":false,"math":{"latex":[],"template":null},"answerTime":0,"id":"68c84b0f776684eb0cdda667","text":"<p><strong>A concerning connection/ Disturbing relevance (Mối liên quan đáng lo ngại)</strong></p>","media":[],"_id":"68c84b0f776684eb0cdda667"}],"explain":{},"hints":[],"kind":"MCQ","marks":{"correct":1,"incorrect":0}},"topics":[],"unifiedStandardIds":[],"cloned":true,"ver":2,"_id":"69ca8be60529b06e80c78c84","time":45000,"type":"MCQ","createdAt":"2026-03-30T14:42:46.239Z","updated":"2026-03-30T14:42:46.252Z","state":"inactive","attempt":0},"69ca8bed4c2a6d0789686804":{"structure":{"settings":{"hasCorrectAnswer":true,"fibDataType":"string","canSubmitCustomResponse":false,"doesOptionHaveMultipleTargets":false,"showAdvancedRTE":false},"hasMath":false,"query":{"type":null,"hasMath":false,"math":{"latex":[],"template":null},"answerTime":-1,"text":"<p>TOPIC: <strong>MOUNTAIN</strong></p><p><strong>Ambition, when unbalanced, can tip into peril. Some climbers, hungry for glory, ignore warnings of storms or the limits of oxygen. Others sacrifice preparation in pursuit of speed. In these cases, the mountain does not forgive. Tales of lives lost remind us that reaching the summit without returning is no success at all. Veterans stress that judgment must guide desire: to value survival over fame, patience over haste. The peaks will remain; it is human strength that proves fragile.</strong></p>","media":[]},"options":[{"type":"text","hasMath":false,"math":{"latex":[],"template":null},"answerTime":0,"id":"68c84a25776684eb0cdda650","text":"<p><strong>Redefining the concept of a mountain/ People’s perspective of mountain (Thay đổi định nghĩa về núi)</strong></p>","media":[],"_id":"68c84a25776684eb0cdda650"},{"type":"text","hasMath":false,"math":{"latex":[],"template":null},"answerTime":0,"id":"68c84a25776684eb0cdda651","text":"<p><strong>The unique feeling of achievement (Cảm giác độc đáo khi đạt đc thành tựu)</strong></p>","media":[],"_id":"68c84a25776684eb0cdda651"},{"type":"text","hasMath":false,"math":{"latex":[],"template":null},"answerTime":0,"id":"68c84a25776684eb0cdda652","text":"<p><strong>Public recognition of accomplishments (Danh tiếng từ thành tựu)</strong></p>","media":[],"_id":"68c84a25776684eb0cdda652"},{"type":"text","hasMath":false,"math":{"latex":[],"template":null},"answerTime":0,"id":"68c84a25776684eb0cdda653","text":"<p><strong>The mistake of misplaced priorities (Sự ưu tiên sai lầm)</strong></p>","media":[],"_id":"68c84a25776684eb0cdda653"},{"type":"text","hasMath":false,"math":{"latex":[],"template":null},"answerTime":0,"id":"68c84b0f776684eb0cdda667","text":"<p><strong>A concerning connection/ Disturbing relevance (Mối liên quan đáng lo ngại)</strong></p>","media":[],"_id":"68c84b0f776684eb0cdda667"}],"explain":{},"hints":[],"kind":"MCQ","marks":{"correct":1,"incorrect":0}},"topics":[],"unifiedStandardIds":[],"cloned":true,"ver":2,"_id":"69ca8bed4c2a6d0789686804","time":45000,"type":"MCQ","createdAt":"2026-03-30T14:42:53.545Z","updated":"2026-03-30T14:42:53.561Z","state":"inactive","attempt":0},"68cc244eb468eb347bcf3306":{"structure":{"settings":{"hasCorrectAnswer":true,"fibDataType":"string","canSubmitCustomResponse":false,"doesOptionHaveMultipleTargets":false,"showAdvancedRTE":false},"hasMath":false,"query":{"type":null,"hasMath":false,"math":{"latex":[],"template":null},"answerTime":-1,"text":"<p>TOPIC: <strong>MOUNTAIN</strong></p><p><strong>Mountains stand tall, but they are not isolated. Glaciers shrink under rising temperatures, altering rivers far below. Tourism scatters waste along trails, pressing fragile plants under careless feet. Local families face shifting harvests and shrinking water supplies. What happens on the slopes echoes far beyond them. Each new footprint connects with a wider chain of consequences, reminding us that climbing is not only about adventure but also about responsibility to a world linked by fragile threads.</strong></p>","media":[]},"options":[{"type":"text","hasMath":false,"math":{"latex":[],"template":null},"answerTime":0,"id":"68c84a25776684eb0cdda650","text":"<p><strong>Redefining the concept of a mountain/ People’s perspective of mountain (Thay đổi định nghĩa về núi)</strong></p>","media":[],"_id":"68c84a25776684eb0cdda650"},{"type":"text","hasMath":false,"math":{"latex":[],"template":null},"answerTime":0,"id":"68c84a25776684eb0cdda651","text":"<p><strong>The unique feeling of achievement (Cảm giác độc đáo khi đạt đc thành tựu)</strong></p>","media":[],"_id":"68c84a25776684eb0cdda651"},{"type":"text","hasMath":false,"math":{"latex":[],"template":null},"answerTime":0,"id":"68c84a25776684eb0cdda652","text":"<p><strong>Public recognition of accomplishments (Danh tiếng từ thành tựu)</strong></p>","media":[],"_id":"68c84a25776684eb0cdda652"},{"type":"text","hasMath":false,"math":{"latex":[],"template":null},"answerTime":0,"id":"68c84a25776684eb0cdda653","text":"<p><strong>The mistake of misplaced priorities (Sự ưu tiên sai lầm)</strong></p>","media":[],"_id":"68c84a25776684eb0cdda653"},{"type":"text","hasMath":false,"math":{"latex":[],"template":null},"answerTime":0,"id":"68c84b0f776684eb0cdda667","text":"<p><strong>A concerning connection/ Disturbing relevance (Mối liên quan đáng lo ngại)</strong></p>","media":[],"_id":"68c84b0f776684eb0cdda667"}],"explain":{},"hints":[],"kind":"MCQ","marks":{"correct":1,"incorrect":0}},"topics":[],"unifiedStandardIds":[],"cloned":true,"ver":2,"_id":"68cc244eb468eb347bcf3306","time":30000,"type":"MCQ","createdAt":"2025-09-18T15:25:02.261Z","updated":"2025-09-18T15:25:36.912Z","state":"inactive","attempt":0},"68cc245e973fcec2353c598f":{"structure":{"settings":{"hasCorrectAnswer":true,"fibDataType":"string","canSubmitCustomResponse":false,"doesOptionHaveMultipleTargets":false,"showAdvancedRTE":false},"hasMath":false,"query":{"type":null,"hasMath":false,"math":{"latex":[],"template":null},"answerTime":-1,"text":"<p>TOPIC: <strong>MOUNTAIN</strong></p><p><strong>Harsh landscapes often draw people closer together. Nights in cold tents foster trust, and shared struggles turn strangers into lifelong friends. Beyond the rope teams, cultures rooted in mountain valleys speak of peaks as sacred guardians, symbols woven into stories and rituals. For many, the relationship is not conquest but coexistence—learning to respect the generosity of the land while acknowledging its dangers. This bond, forged in hardship and tradition, reveals a human need to belong to something larger than ourselves.</strong></p>","media":[]},"options":[{"type":"text","hasMath":false,"math":{"latex":[],"template":null},"answerTime":0,"id":"68c84a25776684eb0cdda650","text":"<p><strong>Redefining the concept of a mountain/ People’s perspective of mountain (Thay đổi định nghĩa về núi)</strong></p>","media":[],"_id":"68c84a25776684eb0cdda650"},{"type":"text","hasMath":false,"math":{"latex":[],"template":null},"answerTime":0,"id":"68c84a25776684eb0cdda651","text":"<p><strong>The unique feeling of achievement (Cảm giác độc đáo khi đạt đc thành tựu)</strong></p>","media":[],"_id":"68c84a25776684eb0cdda651"},{"type":"text","hasMath":false,"math":{"latex":[],"template":null},"answerTime":0,"id":"68c84a25776684eb0cdda652","text":"<p><strong>Public recognition of accomplishments (Danh tiếng từ thành tựu)</strong></p>","media":[],"_id":"68c84a25776684eb0cdda652"},{"type":"text","hasMath":false,"math":{"latex":[],"template":null},"answerTime":0,"id":"68c84a25776684eb0cdda653","text":"<p><strong>Focusing on stability/ sustainability (Tập trung vào sự ổn định)</strong></p>","media":[],"_id":"68c84a25776684eb0cdda653"},{"type":"text","hasMath":false,"math":{"latex":[],"template":null},"answerTime":0,"id":"68c84b0f776684eb0cdda667","text":"<p><strong>A close relationship (Mối quan hệ mật thiết)</strong></p>","media":[],"_id":"68c84b0f776684eb0cdda667"}],"explain":{},"hints":[],"kind":"MCQ","marks":{"correct":1,"incorrect":0}},"topics":[],"unifiedStandardIds":[],"cloned":true,"ver":2,"_id":"68cc245e973fcec2353c598f","time":30000,"type":"MCQ","createdAt":"2025-09-18T15:25:18.198Z","updated":"2025-09-18T15:25:36.912Z","state":"inactive","attempt":0},"68cc246dd09ea458bc69e8a2":{"structure":{"settings":{"hasCorrectAnswer":true,"fibDataType":"string","canSubmitCustomResponse":false,"doesOptionHaveMultipleTargets":false,"showAdvancedRTE":false},"hasMath":false,"query":{"type":null,"hasMath":false,"math":{"latex":[],"template":null},"answerTime":-1,"text":"<p>TOPIC: <strong>MOUNTAIN</strong></p><p><strong>Experienced climbers often say that mountains teach patience more than courage. To face them recklessly is to invite disaster; to return year after year requires steadiness. Stability means careful preparation, physical discipline, and the wisdom to step back when conditions turn. It also extends beyond the slopes—valuing family, health, and community as much as adventure. In a world that prizes extreme records, such balance may seem unremarkable, but it is the quiet foundation of a lifelong relationship with the peaks.</strong></p>","media":[]},"options":[{"type":"text","hasMath":false,"math":{"latex":[],"template":null},"answerTime":0,"id":"68c84a25776684eb0cdda650","text":"<p><strong>Redefining the concept of a mountain/ People’s perspective of mountain (Thay đổi định nghĩa về núi)</strong></p>","media":[],"_id":"68c84a25776684eb0cdda650"},